---
source: crates/clattertrap-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8(out.stdout).unwrap()"
---
Build Rube Goldberg machines with AI models and watch whether they work

Usage: clattertrap <COMMAND>

Commands:
  rules        Print the rules contestants play by, or a JSON Schema
  levels       List every level with its tier and goal
  level        Describe one level in words and JSON
  check        Validate a scene file against its level; exits 1 with the problems
  look         Write a PNG of a scene at the start of its run
  run          Run a scene to its end and print the outcome as JSON
  arena        Run a model through the contestant tools and save every run: Claude Code, or a chat endpoint
  report       Summarize a directory of runs: levels solved per model and arm, attempts, and exclusions
  leaderboard  Levels solved per model and arm over the gallery, ranked; --markdown for the README block
  promote      Copy counted pilot runs into the gallery once their stored outcomes still hold
  verify       Re-simulate every stored outcome under a directory of runs; exits 1 with the mismatches
  mcp          Serve the contestant tools over stdio as an MCP server
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
